x86_64-linux  clang zeroes `Value z = {}` and `Value()` with a call to memset where cxx1 writes the fields out - the difference S-09 recorded in CLAUDE.md ("clang zeroes a nested temporary with a call to memset where cxx1 writes the fields out"), a question about emission and not about a name; the other 16 names agree.
x86_64-windows  the same memset, and the closure of `[this]` in Around::viaLambda, which clang-msvc spells `<lambda_0>` with a deduced return written `@` where cxx1 writes `$_0` and the type - the numbering and spelling lambda.nonames already records. arm64-darwin agrees on all 17 names.
